diff --git a/docs/codex.md b/docs/codex.md
index 0a1b8a2..93b78c5 100644
--- a/docs/codex.md
+++ b/docs/codex.md
@@ -52,6 +52,11 @@ identity includes session ID, task ID, PID and process start time. If the native
 API omits an OS PID, only a unique, marked, exact command match is accepted.
 Missing or ambiguous ownership cannot produce a successful stop.
 
+Literal shell quoting and escaping are parsed when matching an exec-optimized
+program's argv. This includes `python3 -c '...; ...'` after the shell has exited.
+Substitutions, pipelines and expansions are never evaluated or treated as
+literal argv. Multiple matching processes still fail closed.
+
 Before explicit stop/cancel, the supervisor freezes the verified process tree
 and kills it, then verifies absence and reconciles the native API. Freezing is
 necessary: killing `sleep` first can wake Bash and execute its trailing command.
@@ -92,3 +97,7 @@ npm run build
 The full suite includes real Linux child processes, detached descendants,
 ownership ambiguity, duplicate terminal IDs in separate sessions, snapshot races,
 failed tasks, recovery failure and post-stop delayed-write regressions.
+
+The `run-codex` event client uses `readAuthRequirement()` and `eventType` from
+the current adapter API. It closes its session before stopping the app-server,
+and releases the connection on authentication and session-close errors too.
